    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.node_vitality - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.node_vitality.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.node_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Compute the vitality of a single node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.node_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Compute the vitality of a single node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.node_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Compute the vitality of a single node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCompute the vitality of a single node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L75802-L75936){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.node_vitality(\n    node,\n    weighted=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Node vitality](../assets/graphs/node-vitality.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The shared seven-node graph with the queried hub C outlined and its four edges dashed, as if removed. The neighbors can still reach each other around C, so the total pairwise distance only drops from 82 to 70 and the card reads vitality 12.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nNode vitality measures the impact of removing a node on graph connectivity, defined as the\nchange in sum of all pairwise shortest path distances:\n\nvitality(v) = sum_distances(G) - sum_distances(G - v)\n\nWithout weights, distances are hop counts found by breadth-first search; with\n`weighted=True` (the default on a weighted graph) they are path costs summed over edge\nweights. The sum runs\nover ordered pairs of nodes, so on an undirected graph each pair contributes its\ndistance twice; on a directed graph only pairs connected in the direction of the edges\ncontribute. Only finite distances are summed: if removing the node leaves some pairs\nunable to reach each other, those pairs simply drop out of `sum_distances(G - v)`, so the\nresult is always finite. This matches `closeness_vitality()`, which computes the same\nvalue for every node at once.\n\nThe distances to and from the node itself drop out of the total, which raises its\nscore, while pairs that have to detour around it lower the score, so a node whose loss\nforces long detours can score below zero. Vitality is useful for:\n\n- ranking nodes by how much the network's overall reachability depends on them\n- assessing what is lost if a specific station, server, or person drops out\n- comparing a handful of candidate nodes without scoring the whole graph\n\nThe method does not modify the graph.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[node]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node to score, given as an integer node ID or a string label.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, measure distances by edge weight (each edge's weight, `1.0` when unset;\n    the cheapest of parallel edges is used). If `False`, count hops. If `None`\n    (default), follows whether the graph was created as weighted.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The vitality score for the node. Always finite, even when removing the node\n    disconnects the graph. A graph with a single node gives `0.0`.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node does not exist in the graph, or if `weighted=True` and an edge weight is\n    negative.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nVitality is defined as the drop in the network's total pairwise distance caused by\nremoving a single node: $\\mathrm{vit}(v) = W(G) - W(G - v)$, where\n$W(G) = \\sum_{u \\ne w} d(u, w)$ is the Wiener index, summed over reachable pairs\nonly. Removing a cut vertex makes some distances infinite; those pairs are left out\nrather than making the result infinite, so cut vertices tend to score high because\nmany long paths disappear along with them.\n\nBecause computing $W$ requires an all-pairs shortest-path pass (twice: with and\nwithout the node), the cost is $O(V \\cdot (V + E))$ per call. To score every node,\ncall `closeness_vitality()` once rather than looping over this method.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~closeness_vitality`) \n\n:   The vitality of every node at once.\n\n[](`~wiener_index`) \n\n:   The total distance whose change the vitality measures.\n\n[](`~articulation_points`) \n\n:   The nodes whose removal disconnects the graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nOn a 5-node path, the middle node has the highest vitality: removing it splits the path\nin two, and every long distance across the middle drops out of the total. An endpoint\nscores lower, since removing it only shortens the path:\n\n::: {#b124ba21 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(5)\n\npath.node_vitality(3), path.node_vitality(1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(36.0, 20.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe hub of a star lies on every path between leaves, so it outscores any one leaf:\n\n::: {#6559ed6b .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nstar = ec.Graph().add_star_graph(4)\n\nstar.node_vitality(1), star.node_vitality(2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(18.0, 10.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nOn an undirected chain `A - B - C`, removing `B` wipes out all six ordered distances\n(`1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2`). On the directed version, only the three forward pairs are\nconnected, so `B` scores half as much:\n\n::: {#b793cf18 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npairs = [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")]\nchain = ec.Graph.from_edges(pairs)\none_way = ec.Graph.from_edges(pairs, directed=True)\n\nchain.node_vitality(\"B\"), one_way.node_vitality(\"B\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(8.0, 4.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Stations the network can't do without\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, with each stretch of track weighted by its\ntravel time in minutes. Riverside scores highest, since closing it cuts off the harbor,\nand every trip to the harbor drops out of the total. Market scores lowest, and below\nzero: closing it strands no one, but it lengthens so many other trips that the total\ngrows:\n\n::: {#ffa0e054 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nvitality = {n: metro.node_vitality(n) for n in metro.get_node_ids()}\n\nlabel = metro.get_label_from_id\nranked = sorted(vitality, key=vitality.get, reverse=True)\n[label(n) for n in ranked[:2]], [label(n) for n in ranked[-2:]]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(['Riverside', 'Harbor'], ['Old Town', 'Market'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#d7b791db .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.set_node_attrs(\"vitality\", vitality)\nmetro.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"vitality\", color_scale=\"diverging\",\n    color_midpoint=0, label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-887c9664:#b42318;--ect-687b1aa3:#9fb0c4;--ect-f5c642ae:#d0a195;--ect-6cb1fab5:#c15748;--ect-7a8946be:#d2b0a6;--ect-0e851e70:#d3c9c2;--ect-eacb019e:#ce8f82;--ect-05dd5a64:#d1a498;--ect-03796db1:#bc4637;--ect-deae364a:#d3c5bd;--ect-74ab897e:#cf998c;--ect-0f8cd3fc:#d1aca1;--ect-a7b401b0:#d2b2a8;--ect-24583194:#adb9c6;--ect-5360f3ec:#d3c8c0;--ect-45ce4e0c:#4e7ab5;--ect-fcdc0df1:#d09e91;--ect-c00abef8:#d2b3aa;--ect-f13b2e9c:#c35e4f;--ect-374b3d43:#1c5cab;--ect-7814b41d:#4574b3;--ect-86b8d92a:#688cbb;--ect-ceda7692:#8ba3c1;--ect-983d5a39:#afbac7;--ect-087a119b:#d3d1cb;--ect-044e2c76:#ce9385;--ect-e89136d6:#c87263;--ect-5b7ebd3f:#bf5041;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-978968b0:#7d1810;--ect-61e0bd52:#6f7b89;--ect-362f1d55:#917068;--ect-93b7d88b:#873c32;--ect-74cd6f63:#937b74;--ect-0aee408c:#938c87;--ect-cb1e26f1:#90645b;--ect-3e385a4d:#92726a;--ect-9ef8a57a:#833126;--ect-4fa7f50e:#938984;--ect-d9a1597e:#906b62;--ect-79598845:#927870;--ect-43dbe507:#937c75;--ect-895a67a0:#79818a;--ect-ca6267c9:#938c86;--ect-474f4fb0:#36557e;--ect-d0e2d9dd:#916e65;--ect-4617e3ae:#937d76;--ect-079122f1:#884137;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b55